WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.940
What happens when our own staff,
and our own assistants, use AI?

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.180
It can turn on us in four ways.

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.400
First, our secrets go
in and do not come back.

00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:15.645
A colleague puts a contract of forty
pages into a free chatbot for a summary.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:20.520
Free tools typically keep what is typed,
and may use it to train the next model.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:22.490
There is no alert and no log.

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.765
Forbidding the tools does not work.

00:00:25.055 --> 00:00:27.225
The paste moves to a personal phone.

00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:31.113
Second, our assistant takes
orders from a stranger.

00:00:31.478 --> 00:00:35.728
An attacker sends one email with
instructions hidden in white text.

00:00:36.038 --> 00:00:40.348
The assistant cannot tell our
instructions from text it happens to read.

00:00:40.688 --> 00:00:44.478
The more it may send, delete or pay,
the more one email can do.

00:00:45.517 --> 00:00:48.967
Third, the CFO on the
phone is not the CFO.

00:00:49.307 --> 00:00:52.617
A few minutes of public audio
is enough to clone a voice.

00:00:52.967 --> 00:00:55.417
The attacker phones
Finance late on a Friday,

00:00:55.847 --> 00:00:57.517
and urgency is the weapon.

00:00:57.812 --> 00:01:01.002
Voice and video can no
longer prove who someone is.

00:01:01.983 --> 00:01:04.693
Fourth, it sounded right,
and it was made up.

00:01:04.943 --> 00:01:08.873
AI is wrong in exactly the
same tone as when it is right.

00:01:09.173 --> 00:01:13.323
A memo reaches the board table with
a court ruling that does not exist.

00:01:13.738 --> 00:01:16.468
The output is a draft,
like a junior colleague's.

00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:18.827
What good looks like.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:22.062
One approved tool,
with no training on our data.

00:01:22.352 --> 00:01:24.582
AI agents get the access of the task,

00:01:25.132 --> 00:01:28.742
and a person approves anything that sends,
deletes or pays.

00:01:29.147 --> 00:01:32.737
Requests for money by voice are
confirmed on a known number.

00:01:33.107 --> 00:01:37.257
OWASP ranks prompt injection
first in its LLM Top 10.

00:01:37.487 --> 00:01:42.337
And the AI Act, Article 4,
asks us to support staff's AI literacy.

00:01:44.063 --> 00:01:45.273
A suggested first step.

00:01:45.558 --> 00:01:50.468
Start with an inventory of where AI is
used, with what data and what rights.

00:01:50.848 --> 00:01:55.018
Then consider one approved tool
and a usage policy of one page.

00:01:55.398 --> 00:01:56.928
Where to start is your call.

00:01:58.483 --> 00:02:00.453
Four ways AI turns on us.

00:02:00.673 --> 00:02:04.603
Treat the output as a draft,
and everything it reads as untrusted.

